WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.620
Picture a nurse reading

2
00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:02.880
a housing notice.

3
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:03.580
The homes are

4
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.860
for 60% of AMI.

5
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:06.820
So what does that

6
00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.580
mean? AMI stands

7
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.560
for area median income.

8
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:11.440
It's the middle

9
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.500
income for households

10
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:13.540
in a region.

11
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:14.660
Half earn more,

12
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:15.860
half earn less.

13
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:17.020
In the Washington D.C.

14
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.460
area, it's over

15
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:20.820
$150,000 a year

16
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.480
for a family

17
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.540
of four. To keep

18
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:23.660
the math simple,

19
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.920
let's use $150,000.

20
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.180
60% of that

21
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.740
is about $90,000

22
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.380
a year.

23
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:31.340
There's a common rule,

24
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.660
housing is affordable when

25
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.640
it takes no more

26
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.880
than 30% of income.

27
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.000
Here, that's about

28
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.450
$2,250 a month.

29
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.760
80% of AMI,

30
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.500
about $120,000,

31
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.700
serves a different group

32
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.120
with higher rent limits,

33
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.520
so that one number

34
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.160
in a promise

35
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:49.390
really matters.

